{
  "slug": "mongodb-atlas",
  "name": "Mongodb Atlas",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "Connect to MongoDB Atlas clusters only through the Atlas Managed MCP Server. Sign in with your Atlas account to explore data, manage collections, optimize queries, generate reliable code with MongoDB best practices, and manage Atlas resources such as clusters, projects, database users, and network access. If you are running a different MongoDB deployment or want to run a local MongoDB MCP Server, install the MongoDB (Self-Managed MCP) plugin instead.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **6 skills** and **1 MCP server**.\n\n- **Skills** (6): `mongodb-atlas-stream-processing` (Manages MongoDB Atlas Stream Processing (ASP) workflows), `mongodb-connection` (Optimize MongoDB client connection configuration (pools, timeouts, patterns) for any supported driver language), `mongodb-natural-language-querying` (Generate read-only MongoDB queries (find) or aggregation pipelines using natural language, with collection schema context and sample documents), `mongodb-query-optimizer` (Help with MongoDB query optimization and indexing), `mongodb-schema-design` (MongoDB schema design patterns and anti-patterns), `mongodb-search-and-ai` (Guides MongoDB users through implementing and optimizing Atlas Search (full-text), Vector Search (semantic), and Hybrid Search solutions)\n- **MCP servers** (1): `mongodb-atlas`\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install mongodb-atlas@claude-plugins-official` from `mongodb/agent-skills` (`plugins/mongodb-atlas`).",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude",
    "copilot",
    "codex"
  ],
  "pluginType": "package",
  "package": {
    "skill": 6,
    "mcp": 1
  },
  "sourceType": "community",
  "author": {
    "name": "MongoDB"
  },
